meta {
  name: Users - Time zone
  type: http
  seq: 176
}

put {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/user/time-zone
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "time_zone": "Europe/Brussels"
  }
}

docs {
  Set the time zone of the current user (#1476, ADR 0048): an IANA name that PHP knows, like Europe/Brussels or UTC. An unknown name gives 400. Only the member sets it (the platform never changes it) and only the member reads it: it is in the current user (GET /api/v1/user and this answer), never in a resource that another person gets. Without a zone, the zone of the instance applies. Needs user:write.
}
